/Title (The "Black Box" Transparency Problem While the Simple RNN achieved the highest accuracy \(MAPE 1.63%\), it lacks the interpretability of Linear Regression. In a regulated financial environment, the inability to explain why the model predicted a specific price target poses a compliance risk. This trade-off between Performance \(RNN\) and Explainability \(Linear Regression\) necessitates a "Human-in-the-Loop" governance framework, where algorithmic signals are treated as recommendations rather than autonomous execution orders. )
